cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  ATOMICA-Diffusion: conditioning SE(3)-equivariant generative
  design on pretrained interaction representations
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it alongside the
  ATOMICA and DiffSBDD papers listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Emilio Alonso
    family-names: Venegas-Hernandez
    email: emiliovenegas10@gmail.com
    orcid: null
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/EmilioVenegas/ATOMICA-Diffusion-Antibiotic-design
abstract: >-
  An SE(3)-equivariant cross-attention adapter that conditions a
  geometric diffusion model for structure-based drug design
  (DiffSBDD) on per-atom pocket embeddings from ATOMICA, a
  foundation model pretrained on molecular interaction
  interfaces. Both pretrained models are frozen, so the ablation
  isolates the effect of the conditioning signal. Over 100
  held-out CrossDocked pockets the adapter raises median
  drug-likeness (QED +13.9% relative) at a cost in chemical
  diversity (-6.4%).
keywords:
  - structure-based drug design
  - diffusion models
  - SE(3)-equivariance
  - geometric deep learning
  - foundation models
  - antibiotic discovery
license: MIT
